WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:03.993
To cut a useful section of a zebrafish specimen,

00:00:03.993 --> 00:00:07.718
orientation and compatible embedding materials must

00:00:07.718 --> 00:00:08.010
work

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:08.656
together.

00:00:14.175 --> 00:00:17.772
The specimen was oriented in an agarose pre-embedding

00:00:17.772 --> 00:00:21.165
support before subsequent paraffin processing. The

00:00:21.165 --> 00:00:24.626
hoped-for geometry depended on their compatibility.

00:00:31.425 --> 00:00:34.779
Agarose and paraffin did not form the coherent

00:00:34.779 --> 00:00:35.435
embedding

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.440
system the microtome needed.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.424
Material separation frustrated sectioning. There was

00:00:45.424 --> 00:00:45.563
no

00:00:45.563 --> 00:00:49.053
interpretable histological slice from that attempt.

00:00:54.008 --> 00:00:58.190
The images identify an upstream materials bottleneck.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:58.269
A

00:00:58.269 --> 00:01:02.451
changed processing protocol needs its own experimental

00:01:02.451 --> 00:01:03.458
verification.

00:01:09.675 --> 00:01:13.466
This is not a success story about histopathology. It

00:01:13.466 --> 00:01:13.612
is

00:01:13.612 --> 00:01:17.403
the story of what an incompatible preparation taught

00:01:17.403 --> 00:01:17.549
us

00:01:17.549 --> 00:01:18.623
to investigate.
